BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goldcoast-vok4we@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:Rekindle\, Rekindle
DESCRIPTION:Rekindle\, Rekindle is an experimental film by Gold Coast skate
 boarder\, actor\, stunt performer\, artist and filmmaker Sarah Huston. Red
 efining the phrase “skate and destroy\,” Huston reframes skateboarding
 ’s masculine associations with destruction through a cyclical\, regenera
 tive and nurturing feminist lens. Shot on Super 8\, the film follows a ska
 teboarder through a ritual of friction\, motion\, impact and fire. Through
  repetition\, skateboarding becomes a meditation on destruction and creati
 on\, exploring what it means to push the body to its limit\, again and aga
 in. Time: From 10am
LOCATION:HOTA Gallery\, Lower Foyer
URL:https://bleachfestival.com.au/events/bleach-26-rekindle-rekindle
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goldcoast-hl4esz@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:The Butterfly Who Flew Into The Rave
DESCRIPTION:This electrifying performance explores rave culture in a hypnot
 ic hour-long spectacle of pure endurance. This award-winning durational wo
 rk is choreographed to the techno album 'Nocturbulous Behaviour' by Suburb
 an Knights and straddles the border between performance art\, dance\, and 
 theatre. Three dancers are locked in a pattern of relentless movement\, in
  seamless synch\, detailed down to every beat. It’s the come up and the 
 come down all in one - the beauty of feeling alive\, but the consequences 
 that come with it. The dancers embody the obsession of rave culture\, perf
 ectly capturing the communal joy and the physical toll of dancing until yo
 u drop. Indulge in the pain\, the sweat\, the cathartic mess\; a display o
 f pure endurance to achieve a goal. A spectacle of the human body as a vic
 tim to music\, as a victim to passion\, as a victim to our endless desire 
 to achieve more. To win and win again.
LOCATION:Basement
URL:https://bleachfestival.com.au/events/bleach-26-the-butterfly-who-flew-i
 nto-the-rave
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goldcoast-9bp723@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261006
SUMMARY:CYVASA 2.0
DESCRIPTION:CYVASA 2.0 is an experimental dance work by Indonesian and dias
 pora dance artists Juliet Widyasari Burnett and Ishvara Devati\, with a mu
 sic score by Indonesian feminist noise duo Metatesis. In the world of CYVA
 SA 2.0\, ancient Javanese spirituality merges with techno-fantasy aestheti
 cs and glitch distortion. The trans and cis female bodies are dynamic\, sa
 cred entities from this speculative future\, untethered from patriarchal h
 istory. Here\, desire is a driving force that transforms the body’s arch
 itecture - a pulsating\, liquid machine that is continuously upgrading\, r
 eprogrammed and reincarnated. This is not a stage\, but a temple\, laborat
 ory and server room\, where new digital deities are born.
LOCATION:HOTA Gallery 2
URL:https://bleachfestival.com.au/events/bleach-26-cyvasa-2-0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goldcoast-1exdg1f@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261006
SUMMARY:Ocker
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the world premiere of Ocker\, a show in motion from
  leading First Nations company Na Djinang Circus. Ocker is a roving circus
  show tearing through the precinct on a portable railway track built in re
 al time. This modern-day hunting party weaves through crowds\, laying trac
 k wherever the chase leads. Charging forward with single-minded determinat
 ion\, they drag the audience along for the ride. The park becomes a playgr
 ound for strange encounters\, risky acrobatics\, and absurd acts of endura
 nce as circus erupts in the most unexpected places. Improvised scenes cons
 tantly derail the hunt as the troupe negotiates crowds\, obstacles\, and t
 heir own terrible ideas. Swept up in the chaos of the chase\, Ocker waits 
 for nobody. Keeping up is entirely your responsibility.
LOCATION:HOTA Lake Precinct
URL:https://bleachfestival.com.au/events/bleach-26-ocker
END:VEVENT
